    {
        "content": "<p>How can I compile mathlib's tactic? I'm curious how much faster my tactic would be if compiled and not interpreted.</p>\n<p>For example I tried compiling <code>push</code> with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">lean_lib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">precompileModules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">roots</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"ss\">`Mathlib.Tactic.Push</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and then</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Push</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595914850,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1779131369
